.TH "mpvc.conf" "5" "September 2026" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
mpvc.conf - Configuration file for mpvc
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \f[B]mpvc.conf\f[R] file serves as the unified configuration profile
and text layout interface for the \f[C]mpvc(1)\f[R].
.PP
Because the ecosystem is written entirely in POSIX shell scripting, the
configuration file is parsed by directly sourcing it into the
environment during execution.
.PP
The file is divided into clear configuration sections using comment
block headers to group each tool configuration on its own section.
.SH CONFIGURATION SECTIONS
.SS MPVC
.PP
This section defines the mpvc(1) configuration variables.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_MPV\f[B]\f[R]
Defines the executable binary name or path for the core player engine.
Defaults to \f[C]mpv\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_SOCAT\f[B]\f[R]
Defines the executable binary name or path used to stream JSON data over
unix sockets.
Defaults to \f[C]socat\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_LOCAL_CACHE\f[B]\f[R]
Boolean flag switch (\f[C]true\f[R] or \f[C]false\f[R]) controlling
whether regional caching routines are activated during playback
sequences.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_FMTSTR\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_FMTSTR_LOFI\f[B]\f[R]
Customizes the output of the \f[C]mpvc [status]\f[R] command to display
a summary of the mpv playing state, shown by the rest of tools.
.SS Formatting String Tokens
.PP
The status strings (\f[C]MPVC_FMTSTR\f[R] and
\f[C]MPVC_FMTSTR_LOFI\f[R]) parse the following tokens dynamically at
runtime to generate the \f[C]mpvc [status]\f[R] terminal layout view:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%status%\f[R] : Active player state icon or text (e.g., Playing,
Paused).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%statuslofi%\f[R] : Stream-specific processing states.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%title%\f[R] : Metadata title track string of the current media
file.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%percentage%%\f[R] : Numerical percentage tracking playback
progress.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%length%\f[R] : Total temporal duration length of the active track
asset.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%position%\f[R] : Index tracking the numerical item number of the
track.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%playlistlength%\f[R] : Cumulative count tracking total track
objects in queue.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%=chapter%\f[R] : Numeric label naming the current playing chapter
layer.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]/%chapters%\f[R] : Total embedded chapter segments discovered in
media container.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%mutelofi%\f[R] : Toggle status indicator flagging audio muting
behaviors.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%volume%%\f[R] : Current audio speaker sound level gain percentage
metrics.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%shufflelofi%\f[R] : Tracks if random shuffling behaviors are
enabled.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%ablooplofi%\f[R] : Displays segment loop hooks.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%singlelofi%\f[R] : Tracks if a single file loop freeze constraint
is active.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%repeatlofi%\f[R] : Tracks if playlist wrapper re-looping sequences
are active.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%idlelofi%\f[R] : Displays if player engines are idling without an
active container.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]%videolofi%\f[R] : Video layer processing status symbols.
.SS MPVC-TUI
.PP
This section configures terminal environment variables and scaling
preferences for the terminal visual frontend interface
\f[B]mpvc-tui\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_TUI_TERM\f[B]\f[R]
Declares the explicit target shell terminal application spawned
specifically when launching graphical console configurations in detached
windows.
.SS MPVC-FZF
.PP
This section contains option flags, remote scraping node overrides, and
execution properties for the interactive search interface
\f[B]mpvc-fzf\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_TERM\f[B]\f[R]
Defines the system terminal emulator tool launched to spawn detached
windows when passing the selection flag \f[C]-x\f[R] or
\f[C]launch\f[R].
Defaults to \f[C]xterm\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_FZF_INVID_URL\f[B]\f[R]
Stores your preferred URL address link pointing to a public or
self-hosted \f[B]Invidious\f[R] API instance mirror node to handle
global text lookups.
.SS MPVC-WEB
.PP
This section handles server port rules, encryption endpoints, UI refresh
behaviors, and thumbnail parsing switches for the local HTTP daemon
interface controller \f[B]mpvc-web\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_WEB_PORT\f[B]\f[R]
Specifies the default plaintext HTTP listening network port assigned to
the web gateway server daemon.
Defaults to \f[C]8888\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_WEB_SSL_PORT\f[B]\f[R]
Declares the network port assigned to handle secure, encrypted HTTPS
client browser connections.
Defaults to \f[C]8443\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_WEB_THUMBNAIL_ENABLE\f[B]\f[R]
Boolean flag switch (\f[C]true\f[R] or \f[C]false\f[R]) controlling
whether the web frontend interface actively pulls, parses, and shows
media artwork thumbnail images over the network dashboard.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]MPVC_WEB_HTML_REFRESH\f[B]\f[R]
Establishes a time interval integer (measured in seconds) instructing
client web browsers how frequently to automatically reload the page
interface state to stay synchronized with track changes.
Defaults to \f[C]240\f[R].
